    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d46-a1">

                <pb facs="0134" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg46"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mérey to Mr. Storer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial and Royal Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1904-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14,
                                1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reply to the highly esteemed note of the 2d instant the Imperial and Royal
                    ministry of foreign affairs has the honor most respectfully to bring to the <pb
                        facs="0135" n="47" xml:id="pg47"/> knowledge of his excellency the
                    ambassador of the United States of America, Mr. Bellamy Storer, that the
                    Imperial and Royal Government awaits with pleasure the intended visit to the
                    ports of Trieste and Fiume by an American squadron consisting of nine ships.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself at the same time of this opportunity to renew,
                    etc.</p>
                <closer>For the minister. <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Mérey.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
